    "introductoryText": "Working-day arithmetic that knows about **public holidays**, not just weekends:\n\n- **Count** the working days between a start and an end date (for example raised and resolved)\n- **Add** N working days to a date to get a **due date** (N from a field, such as an SLA per priority, or a fixed number)\n- With both, an **SLA check**: *Met Target* yes / no and *Working Days Late*\n\nPublic holidays are generated by rule, for any year, for **England and Wales**, **Scotland**, **Northern Ireland** (bank holidays, with substitute days and the one-off UK holidays since 2011 such as jubilees, the coronation and the state funeral) or the **US** (federal holidays, observed dates). Add your own closure dates (office shutdowns, company days) and choose the weekend (Saturday and Sunday, Friday and Saturday, Sunday only, or none).\n\nThe second output lists every holiday used, so the calendar can be checked or reused.\n\nOmniscope's NETWORKDAYS formula counts weekdays only; this block adds holidays, due dates and SLA checks.",
